      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Why not do the avatar performance scan server side ? One time after uploading ? \nWant to save resources ?\nOk then do it \"crowd computed\" by different clients, and let them vote over it. And then save the result to the server along with the other avatar meta data.\nYou can even optimize the \"crowd computing\": let the SDK compute a performance level and save it as \"claimed performance level\" (can be faked ofc with modified SDK). Then let the crowd compute the real performance level only, when the avatar \"should be displayed\" according to the \"claimed level\" and the clients performance settings.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
